From: TB520FU port maintainers
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: tb520fu: define board oscillator rates

The generic SM8650 DTS leaves oscillator rates to the board. Without
clock-frequency the fixed-clock provider returns -EIO. The TB520FU DTBs
omitted both rates, leaving downstream clocks without reference sources.
Observed failures include empty CPU OPP tables, VIDEO_CC PLL timeouts
and USB PHY initialization errors. Use stock running.dts rates: XO is
76800000 Hz and sleep_clk is 32000 Hz, shared by Tianma and BOE boards.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu.dtsi
@@ -12,6 +12,15 @@
 #include "pm8550ve.dtsi"
 #include "pm8550vs.dtsi"
 #include "pmk8550.dtsi"
+
+/* Board oscillators from the stock TB520FU running device tree. */
+&xo_board {
+	clock-frequency = <76800000>;
+};
+
+&sleep_clk {
+	clock-frequency = <32000>;
+};
 
 /delete-node/ &rmtfs_mem;
 /delete-node/ &hwfence_shbuf;
